# Findings this repository cannot act on, with a date by which it must look
# again. Never a permanent suppression: an entry with no expiry is how a report
# stops being read.
#
# The runtime base is mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0-noble-chiseled. A
# chiseled image has no package manager and no shell, which is most of why it
# was chosen — and it also means there is no `apt-get upgrade` to run here. The
# glibc these name is whatever Microsoft built the image with, and the only way
# to a patched one is Microsoft publishing a rebuilt image.
#
# Ubuntu fixed all six in libc6 2.39-0ubuntu8.9; the image ships 2.39-0ubuntu8.8.
# They are denial-of-service and memory-safety faults in iconv conversion, tilde
# expansion, wordexp, tdelete and strfmon — none of them on a path this app
# reaches with anything a request controls, which is why waiting is tolerable
# rather than merely convenient.
#
# CVE-2026-84782 is the same situation in OpenSSL: Ubuntu fixed it in
# 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16, and the newest image (built 2026-09-04, checked
# 2026-10-01) still ships libssl3t64 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.15. It is a heap read in
# DTLS handshake retransmission. DTLS is TLS over datagrams, and .NET never
# speaks it: every TLS connection this app makes — Postgres, imports, the
# assistant's providers — is over TCP.
#
# When this expires: rebuild and look. If Microsoft has shipped the newer glibc
# the scan passes on its own and these lines can go. If it has not, extend the
# date deliberately, here, with today's reasoning.
CVE-2026-80489 exp:2026-10-19
CVE-2026-77117 exp:2026-10-19
CVE-2026-6791 exp:2026-10-19
CVE-2026-6368 exp:2026-10-19
CVE-2026-19542 exp:2026-10-19
CVE-2026-19499 exp:2026-10-19
CVE-2026-84782 exp:2026-10-19
